      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "unlZA",
      "text": "16",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Suppose temperature of $\\mathrm{Sun}=T$\r\nWhen it is doubled, $T^{\\prime}=2 T$\r\nFrom law of radiation (Stefan's law)\r\n$$\r\nE \\propto T^{4}=\\sigma T^{4}\r\n$$\r\n$\\sigma=$ Stefan's constant.\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\nE_{1}=T^{4} \\\\\r\nE_{2} \\approx(2 \\Pi)^{4} \\\\\r\n\\frac{E_{1}}{E_{2}}=\\frac{T^{4}}{2^{4} \\cdot T^{4}} \\\\\r\nE_{2}=16 E_{1}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
